Z||000004||StuGood||12-25-2001||04:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by CoolBlue87GT:<BR><B>...The finish looked like it was painted outside, and a sand storm came up...Good news, it was a bad dream.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I took my 1986 gold SE to one of the local Pontiac dealership to have it repaired & repainted(other party's fault- their insurance paid for the damage to my car).  The body shop man told me that he'd work my car in.  They had been booked all of the previous week to repair the finish on a bunch of the new cars that were sitting in the lot.  Apparently, a bunch of concrete sealer blew across onto the (brand new) cars in the lot, from the construction being done to the highway just to the south of the dealership.  What a real-life nightmare  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">!<P>I looked at him, a bit apprehensively, and I guess it showed.  He smiled and said, "Don't worry- we'll be keeping your car <B>inside</B>!||||reg||7
